  "output": "## Test Coverage Analysis — Platizio NextGen\n\n**Current state: zero test coverage.** No test runner is installed (`package.json` has no `test` script, no `vitest`/`jest`/`@testing-library/*`/`playwright` in dependencies), and there isn't a single `*.test.*`/`*.spec.*` file anywhere in `src/`. This is a Next.js 16 + React 19 marketing site (~25 components), mostly presentational, but it has a meaningful amount of pure logic and stateful behavior hidden inside \"just UI\" files that currently has no safety net at all.\n\nPer this project's own `node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/02-guides/testing/`, Next 16 officially supports **Vitest + React Testing Library** for unit/component tests and **Playwright** for E2E — I'll base skeletons on that stack since it matches the installed Next.js version.\n\n### 0. Foundational gap: no test infrastructure exists\n\n```\nnpm install -D vitest @vitejs/plugin-react jsdom @testing-library/react @testing-library/dom @testing-library/jest-dom vite-tsconfig-paths\n```\n\n```ts\n// vitest.config.mts\nimport { defineConfig } from \"vitest/config\";\nimport react from \"@vitejs/plugin-react\";\nimport tsconfigPaths from \"vite-tsconfig-paths\";\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [tsconfigPaths(), react()],\n  test: {\n    environment: \"jsdom\",\n    setupFiles: [\"./vitest.setup.ts\"],\n    globals: true,\n  },\n});\n```\n\n```ts\n// vitest.setup.ts\nimport \"@testing-library/jest-dom/vitest\";\n```\n\n```json\n// package.json — add\n\"scripts\": { \"test\": \"vitest\", \"test:e2e\": \"playwright test\" }\n```\n\n---\n\n### 1. `src/lib/products.tsx` — `getProduct()` / `PRODUCT_MAP` (lines 517–526)\n\n**Untested, and currently has zero consumers anywhere in `src/`** — there's no `/products/[slug]` route yet, so this is public API surface that will silently break the moment a page starts using it, with no test to catch it.\n\nGaps: unknown slug → `undefined` (no throw, no fallback UI contract defined), case sensitivity (`\"SIF\"` vs `\"sif\"`), empty string, `PRODUCT_MAP` completeness/uniqueness, every `product.tag` resolving to a real `PRODUCT_GLYPHS` key.\n\n```ts\n// src/lib/products.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { PRODUCTS, PRODUCT_MAP, getProduct, RISK_DISCLAIMER } from \"@/lib/products\";\nimport { PRODUCT_GLYPHS } from \"@/lib/productGlyphs\";\n\ndescribe(\"getProduct\", () => {\n  it(\"returns the matching product for a valid slug\", () => {\n    expect(getProduct(\"sif\")?.name).toBe(\"Specialised Investment Funds\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns undefined for an unknown slug\", () => {\n    expect(getProduct(\"not-a-real-slug\")).toBeUndefined();\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns undefined for empty string\", () => {\n    expect(getProduct(\"\")).toBeUndefined();\n  });\n\n  it(\"is case-sensitive (documents current behavior)\", () => {\n    expect(getProduct(\"SIF\")).toBeUndefined();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"PRODUCTS data integrity\", () => {\n  it(\"has unique slugs\", () => {\n    const slugs = PRODUCTS.map((p) => p.slug);\n    expect(new Set(slugs).size).toBe(slugs.length);\n  });\n\n  it(\"every product.tag resolves to a real glyph\", () => {\n    for (const p of PRODUCTS) {\n      expect(PRODUCT_GLYPHS[p.tag]).toBeDefined();\n    }\n  });\n\n  it(\"PRODUCT_MAP contains every product from PRODUCTS\", () => {\n    for (const p of PRODUCTS) {\n      expect(PRODUCT_MAP[p.slug]).toBe(p);\n    }\n  });\n\n  it(\"RISK_DISCLAIMER is non-empty\", () => {\n    expect(RISK_DISCLAIMER.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. `waveY()` in `MarketConstellation.tsx` (lines 26–32)\n\nPure deterministic math function driving the WebGL terrain — completely untested, and the only part of that file that *can* be unit-tested without a WebGL context.\n\n```ts\n// src/components/three/waveY.test.ts (extract waveY as a named export first)\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { waveY } from \"@/components/three/MarketConstellation\";\n\ndescribe(\"waveY\", () => {\n  it(\"is deterministic for the same inputs\", () => {\n    expect(waveY(1, 2, 3)).toBe(waveY(1, 2, 3));\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns 0-ish at the origin with t=0\", () => {\n    expect(waveY(0, 0, 0)).toBeCloseTo(0, 5);\n  });\n\n  it(\"stays within the expected amplitude envelope\", () => {\n    for (let x = -12; x <= 12; x += 1) {\n      for (let t = 0; t < 20; t += 1) {\n        expect(Math.abs(waveY(x, 0, t))).toBeLessThan(1); // sum of amplitudes ~0.74\n      }\n    }\n  });\n});\n```\n*(Currently `waveY` isn't exported — that itself is a gap: extract-and-export it so it's testable in isolation instead of only reachable through a `useFrame` callback inside a Canvas.)*\n\n---\n\n### 3. `Preloader.tsx` — progress easing & \"fires once\" guarantee (lines 21–61)\n\nNo test covers: the eased progress counter reaching exactly 100, the `doneRef` de-dupe guard (`onDone` must fire **exactly once** even if the effect re-runs because `onDone` isn't memoized by the caller), the reduced-motion fast path, or the `document.documentElement.style.overflow` cleanup on unmount.\n\n```tsx\n// src/components/Preloader.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi, afterEach } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, screen, cleanup } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport Preloader from \"@/components/Preloader\";\n\nafterEach(cleanup);\n\ndescribe(\"Preloader\", () => {\n  it(\"calls onDone exactly once and hides itself when progress completes\", async () => {\n    const onDone = vi.fn();\n    render(<Preloader onDone={onDone} />);\n    // advance rAF/timers to completion...\n    expect(onDone).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);\n  });\n\n  it(\"resets document overflow on unmount even mid-animation\", () => {\n    const onDone = vi.fn();\n    const { unmount } = render(<Preloader onDone={onDone} />);\n    expect(document.documentElement.style.overflow).toBe(\"hidden\");\n    unmount();\n    expect(document.documentElement.style.overflow).toBe(\"\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"skips the counter and resolves immediately under prefers-reduced-motion\", () => {\n    // mock useReducedMotion / matchMedia to reduced=true\n    const onDone = vi.fn();\n    render(<Preloader onDone={onDone} />);\n    expect(onDone).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. `IntroProvider.tsx` / `useIntroDone()` — default vs provided context\n\n`createContext(true)` means `useIntroDone()` returns `true` by default **outside** any provider (relied on by `SiteShell.tsx`'s comment), but `false` until `Preloader.onDone` fires **inside** `IntroProvider`. That default-vs-provided distinction is exactly the kind of thing a refactor silently breaks.\n\n```tsx\n// src/components/IntroProvider.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, screen, act } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { IntroProvider, useIntroDone } from \"@/components/IntroProvider\";\n\nfunction Probe() {\n  return <span>{String(useIntroDone())}</span>;\n}\n\ndescribe(\"useIntroDone\", () => {\n  it(\"defaults to true when used outside a provider\", () => {\n    render(<Probe />);\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"true\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n\n  it(\"is false inside IntroProvider until the preloader completes\", () => {\n    render(\n      <IntroProvider>\n        <Probe />\n      </IntroProvider>,\n    );\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"false\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. `Journey.tsx` — scroll-progress → active-step clamp (lines 61–65)\n\n```js\nMath.max(0, Math.min(STEPS.length - 1, Math.floor(v * STEPS.length)))\n```\nNo test covers the boundaries: `v = 0`, `v = 1` (must clamp to `STEPS.length - 1`, not `STEPS.length`), and — this is the real gap — **`v` being `NaN`** (e.g. if `scrollYProgress` ever emits `NaN` during layout thrash) propagates through `Math.floor`/`Math.min`/`Math.max` untouched, so `active` becomes `NaN` and `STEPS[NaN]` is `undefined`, silently breaking the highlighted-step UI with no error thrown.\n\n```ts\n// extract the clamp as a pure helper to make it testable:\n// export function stepIndexFor(v: number, count: number) { ... }\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { stepIndexFor } from \"@/components/sections/Journey\";\n\ndescribe(\"stepIndexFor\", () => {\n  it.each([\n    [0, 0],\n    [0.999, 2],\n    [1, 2],       // must clamp, not overflow to STEPS.length\n    [-0.5, 0],    // defensive: negative progress\n  ])(\"clamps %f to index %i\", (v, expected) => {\n    expect(stepIndexFor(v, 3)).toBe(expected);\n  });\n\n  it(\"does not produce NaN for NaN input (currently fails — bug)\", () => {\n    expect(Number.isNaN(stepIndexFor(NaN, 3))).toBe(false);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. `MagneticButton.tsx` — pointer-move math & input-type gating (lines 43–53)\n\nNo coverage for: touch/pen input being intentionally ignored (`e.pointerType !== \"mouse\"`), the `reduce`-motion early-return, missing-ref guard, or that `onLeave` always resets to `(0, 0)` regardless of motion preference.\n\n```tsx\n// src/components/ui/MagneticButton.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, fireEvent } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { MagneticButton } from \"@/components/ui/MagneticButton\";\n\ndescribe(\"MagneticButton\", () => {\n  it(\"renders an <a> when href is given, a <button> otherwise\", () => {\n    const { rerender, container } = render(<MagneticButton href=\"/x\">Go</MagneticButton>);\n    expect(container.querySelector(\"a\")).not.toBeNull();\n    rerender(<MagneticButton onClick={() => {}}>Go</MagneticButton>);\n    expect(container.querySelector(\"button\")).not.toBeNull();\n  });\n\n  it(\"ignores touch pointer events for the magnetic offset\", () => {\n    // fire a pointermove with pointerType \"touch\" and assert transform stays at 0\n  });\n\n  it(\"calls onClick when the button variant is pressed\", () => {\n    const onClick = vi.fn();\n    const { getByText } = render(<MagneticButton onClick={onClick}>Go</MagneticButton>);\n    fireEvent.click(getByText(\"Go\"));\n    expect(onClick).toHaveBeenCalledOnce();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 7. `Reveal.tsx` — `RevealWords` word-splitting & accent matching\n\nNo coverage for: empty string input (`\"\".split(\" \")` → `[\"\"]`, renders one blank span), accent words that don't appear in `text` (silently no-op — fine, but undocumented), and — an actual a11y inconsistency worth pinning down — the animated path sets `aria-label={text}` with `aria-hidden` on every word span (so screen readers read the label once), but the `reduce`-motion fallback path renders plain `<span>` words with **no `aria-label`**, so a screen reader under reduced motion reads each word individually including the injected `\" \"` — different accessible output depending on OS setting.\n\n```tsx\n// src/components/ui/Reveal.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { RevealWords, FadeUp } from \"@/components/ui/Reveal\";\n\ndescribe(\"RevealWords\", () => {\n  it(\"renders each word of the text\", () => {\n    render(<RevealWords text=\"Hello brave world\" />);\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"Hello\", { exact: false })).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n\n  it(\"applies accentClassName only to words in the accent list\", () => {\n    const { container } = render(\n      <RevealWords text=\"Plan ahead\" accent={[\"ahead\"]} accentClassName=\"italic\" />,\n    );\n    expect(container.querySelector(\".italic\")?.textContent).toBe(\"ahead\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"handles empty text without throwing\", () => {\n    expect(() => render(<RevealWords text=\"\" />)).not.toThrow();\n  });\n\n  it(\"exposes the same accessible name under reduced motion as under animation (currently fails)\", () => {\n    // render once with matchMedia mocked reduced=true, once reduced=false,\n    // assert screen.getByLabelText / accessible text matches in both\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"FadeUp\", () => {\n  it(\"renders children as a plain div under reduced motion (no motion wrapper)\", () => {\n    // mock useReducedMotion -> true, assert no `style` transform attrs applied\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 8. `Products.tsx` — hover/focus preview state machine (lines 197–207)\n\n`onDeactivate` clears `activeIndex` but **intentionally never resets `previewIndex`**, so the sticky preview panel keeps showing the last-hovered product after mouse-leave. That's presumably intended design, but it's unverified behavior that a future refactor could accidentally \"fix\" into a regression. Keyboard `onFocus`/`onBlur` wiring to the same handlers as mouse hover is also untested.\n\n```tsx\n// src/components/sections/Products.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, fireEvent, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport Products from \"@/components/sections/Products\";\n\ndescribe(\"Products\", () => {\n  it(\"keeps showing the last-hovered product in the preview after mouseleave\", () => {\n    render(<Products />);\n    const row = screen.getByText(\"Mutual Funds\").closest(\"a\")!;\n    fireEvent.mouseEnter(row);\n    fireEvent.mouseLeave(row);\n    // preview panel (desktop) should still show \"Mutual Funds\", not revert to index 0\n  });\n\n  it(\"activates the same row via keyboard focus as via mouse hover\", () => {\n    render(<Products />);\n    const row = screen.getByText(\"Portfolio Management Services\").closest(\"a\")!;\n    fireEvent.focus(row);\n    // assert active styling / preview index updated\n    fireEvent.blur(row);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 9. `Nav.tsx` — scroll threshold, mobile menu, `overflow` side effect\n\nNo coverage for: `scrolled` flipping at exactly `scrollY = 48`, mobile menu `open` toggling `document.documentElement.style.overflow` to `\"hidden\"`/`\"\"`, that overflow is reset when the component unmounts while the menu is open (currently the cleanup only depends on `open`, so unmounting mid-open leaves `overflow: hidden` on the page — **likely bug**), and `aria-expanded`/`aria-label` toggling correctly.\n\n```tsx\n// src/components/Nav.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, fireEvent, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport Nav from \"@/components/Nav\";\n\ndescribe(\"Nav\", () => {\n  it(\"opens the mobile menu and sets aria-expanded/body overflow\", () => {\n    render(<Nav />);\n    const toggle = screen.getByLabelText(\"Open menu\");\n    fireEvent.click(toggle);\n    expect(screen.getByLabelText(\"Close menu\")).toHaveAttribute(\"aria-expanded\", \"true\");\n    expect(document.documentElement.style.overflow).toBe(\"hidden\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"restores overflow when the menu is closed\", () => {\n    render(<Nav />);\n    fireEvent.click(screen.getByLabelText(\"Open menu\"));\n    fireEvent.click(screen.getByLabelText(\"Close menu\"));\n    expect(document.documentElement.style.overflow).toBe(\"\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"restores overflow on unmount even while the menu is still open (currently fails — bug)\", () => {\n    const { unmount } = render(<Nav />);\n    fireEvent.click(screen.getByLabelText(\"Open menu\"));\n    unmount();\n    expect(document.documentElement.style.overflow).toBe(\"\");\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 10. Duplicated `TICKS` geometry generator (`CTA.tsx`, `ContactCTA.tsx`) & `Trust.tsx`/`AboutPage.tsx` `ticks()`\n\nSame trig computation is duplicated in two files (`CTA.tsx:8-18` and `ContactCTA.tsx:8-18`) with a comment explicitly calling out an SSR/CSR hydration invariant (\"so server and client render identical markup\") — that invariant has no test, and the duplication means a future edit to one copy silently diverges from the other.\n\n```ts\n// after extracting into a shared src/lib/ticks.ts:\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { buildCompassTicks } from \"@/lib/ticks\";\n\ndescribe(\"buildCompassTicks\", () => {\n  it(\"produces the same output on repeated calls (SSR/CSR hydration safety)\", () => {\n    expect(buildCompassTicks()).toEqual(buildCompassTicks());\n  });\n\n  it(\"rounds coordinates to 2 decimal places\", () => {\n    for (const t of buildCompassTicks()) {\n      for (const v of [t.x1, t.y1, t.x2, t.y2]) {\n        expect(v).toBe(Math.round(v * 100) / 100);\n      }\n    }\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### Missing error-handling coverage\n\nThere is essentially **no explicit error handling anywhere** in the app (no error boundaries, no try/catch, no `notFound()`/`error.tsx`), which is itself a gap worth flagging rather than testing around:\n- No `src/app/error.tsx` or `not-found.tsx` — an unhandled render error in any section crashes the whole page with the default Next.js error overlay. **Test**: add `error.tsx`, then a test asserting it renders when a child throws.\n- `getProduct()` returns `undefined` silently with no consumer-side guard yet — once a `/products/[slug]/page.tsx` is added, it must call `notFound()` for an unknown slug; that page doesn't exist yet, so there's nothing to test today, but it's the single highest-risk near-term gap given `lib/products.tsx` is otherwise complete.\n- `Image` components in `AboutPage.tsx` (team photos, founder photo) have no `onError` fallback — a missing/renamed file under `public/about/` fails silently to a broken image with no test pinning expected `alt` fallback behavior.\n\n### Integration/E2E gaps (Playwright)\n\nNone of the following cross-component flows are covered at all:\n- Preloader → Nav/Hero entrance choreography on the homepage (`IntroProvider` wiring end-to-end)\n- Smooth-scroll anchor navigation (`/#products`, `/#journey`, `/#trust`, `/#contact`) actually landing on the right section\n- Mobile nav open → click a link → menu closes → page scrolls to target\n- `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` end-to-end: every animated component (10+) branches on it, but no E2E run ever exercises that OS setting\n- `/about` route rendering without the homepage preloader (per `SiteShell.tsx`'s comment) — currently unverified\n- Responsive breakpoints (`lg:` grid switches in `Products.tsx`/`Journey.tsx` change entire interaction model between mobile and desktop)\n\n```ts\n// e2e/homepage.spec.ts\nimport { test, expect } from \"@playwright/test\";\n\ntest(\"preloader lifts and homepage becomes interactive\", async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.goto(\"/\");\n  await expect(page.getByText(\"Platizio\")).toBeVisible();\n  await page.getByRole(\"link\", { name: \"Book a Consultation\" }).first().click();\n});\n\ntest(\"respects prefers-reduced-motion\", async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.emulateMedia({ reducedMotion: \"reduce\" });\n  await page.goto(\"/\");\n  // assert no preloader curtain, sections visible immediately\n});\n\ntest(\"mobile menu closes after navigating\", async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.setViewportSize({ width: 390, height: 844 });\n  await page.goto(\"/\");\n  await page.getByLabel(\"Open menu\").click();\n  await page.getByRole(\"link\", { name: \"About\" }).click();\n  await expect(page).toHaveURL(/\\/about/);\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### Priority summary\n\n| Priority | Gap | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| P0 | No test infra at all | Nothing else is possible until Vitest/Playwright are wired in |\n| P0 | `getProduct`/`PRODUCT_MAP` | Public API, zero consumers today, will break silently when product pages ship |\n| P1 | `Nav.tsx` overflow-leak on unmount-while-open | Real bug candidate, breaks page scroll for users |\n| P1 | `Journey.tsx` `NaN` clamp | Real bug candidate, silent UI breakage |\n| P1 | Reduced-motion branch across ~10 components | Large untested surface, accessibility-relevant, legally adjacent for a regulated-finance site |\n| P2 | `waveY`, tick-generator pure functions | Cheap, high-value unit tests once extracted/exported |\n| P2 | `Preloader` once-only `onDone` guarantee | Silent double-fire would desync intro choreography |\n| P3 | Full E2E flows | Valuable but only worth it once component-level coverage exists |\n",
